<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
{% include "head.liquid" %}
<body>
  {% include "header.liquid" %}

  {%- comment -%}
    A page opts into the wide list measure with `wide: true` under `data:` in
    its front matter. Cobalt's front matter is a closed schema — a bare custom
    key fails the build with "unknown field" — so `data` is the sanctioned
    place for this.

    It must be TESTED, never interpolated. Printing page.data.wide on a page
    that doesn't set it is a hard build error ("requested index=wide,
    available indexes="); testing it reads falsy and is safe. Same asymmetry
    the paginator guards in tags.liquid and the featured_count guard in
    post-list.liquid rely on.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <main class="content-section">
    <div class="content-inner{% if page.data.wide %} content-inner--wide{% endif %}">
      {{ page.content }}
    </div>
  </main>

  {% include "footer.liquid" %}
</body>
</html>
